---
/**
 * ResearchArchitecture.astro — 3 Core Theoretical Modules from Bernard's PhD Dissertation
 * Synthesizes FedM3 Optimizer, Continuous Memory System (CMS-TTT), and HOPE-FL Architecture.
 */
---

<section class="section research-architecture-section" aria-labelledby="arch-heading">
  <div class="sdr-section-title-row">
    <div>
      <h2 id="arch-heading" class="sdr-section-title">
        PROPOSED ARCHITECTURAL MODULES // NOVEL CONTRIBUTIONS
      </h2>
      <p class="section-micro-desc">
        Three-tier framework engineered to resolve catastrophic forgetting, gradient explosion, and
        edge privacy bottlenecks
      </p>
    </div>
    <span class="sdr-station-count-badge">3 SYSTEM MODULES</span>
  </div>

  <div class="modules-stack">
    <!-- ── MODULE 01 ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="module-card">
      <div class="dev-card-corner-tl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="dev-card-corner-br" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="module-header">
        <div class="module-meta">
          <span class="module-number">MODULE #01</span>
          <span class="module-badge">ADAPTIVE AGGREGATION</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="module-name">FedM3: Federated Multi-Scale Momentum Muon Optimizer</h3>
        <p class="module-lead">
          Dynamic parameter orthogonalization replacing coordinate-wise heuristic updates with
          quintic Newton-Schulz polar iterations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="module-body-grid">
        <div class="module-feature-col">
          <h4 class="feature-title">THEORETICAL MECHANISM</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">
            Standard adaptive optimizers (Adam, RMSprop) require storing and transmitting full
            momentum matrices, which doubles client communication payload. FedM3 implements a
            matrix-valued optimizer that directly updates 2D parameter weights via their polar
            factor:
          </p>
          <div class="module-formula-box">
            <code>&Delta;W_orth = NS_5(M_t) &middot; &eta;</code>
            <span class="formula-caption">
              where NS_5 is a 5-step quintic Newton-Schulz iteration computing the matrix sign
              function.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="module-feature-col">
          <h4 class="feature-title">ENGINEERING ADVANTAGES</h4>
          <ul class="module-bullet-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Bounded Spectral Updates:</strong> Enforces unit spectral norm updates
              ($||\Delta W||_2 \le 1$), inherently preventing gradient explosion under non-IID
              conditions.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>No Communication Doubling:</strong> Operates entirely on the client gradient
              buffer without requiring second-moment accumulator transmission.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Zero Client Sorting:</strong> Outperforms FedMedian and FedTrimmedMean without
              introducing cryptographic sorting overhead under SMPC.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── MODULE 02 ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="module-card">
      <div class="dev-card-corner-tl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="dev-card-corner-br" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="module-header">
        <div class="module-meta">
          <span class="module-number">MODULE #02</span>
          <span class="module-badge">CONTINUAL MEMORY</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="module-name">Continuous Memory System (CMS) for Test-Time Training (TTT)</h3>
        <p class="module-lead">
          Treating historical context retention as an online self-supervised meta-learning task
          rather than rigid parameter freezing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="module-body-grid">
        <div class="module-feature-col">
          <h4 class="feature-title">CATASTROPHIC FORGETTING MITIGATION</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">
            Elastic Weight Consolidation (EWC) and memory-replay methods fail in decentralized
            networks due to privacy policies (cannot store past patient data) and bandwidth limits
            (Fisher Information matrices exceed model weights). CMS equips the foundation model with
            an internal meta-memory loop:
          </p>
          <div class="module-formula-box">
            <code>
              W_t^(mem) = W_&#123;t - 1&#125;^(mem) - &eta;_inner &nabla; L_self(x_t; W_&#123;t -
              1&#125;^(mem))
            </code>
            <span class="formula-caption">
              Online gradient descent compressing sequential context directly into expressive hidden
              state weights.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="module-feature-col">
          <h4 class="feature-title">NEURAL ARCHITECTURAL SYNERGY</h4>
          <ul class="module-bullet-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Sliding-Window Polynomial Mapping:</strong> Prevents overwriting of older
              synaptic representations during long-horizon fine-tuning.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Zero Raw Data Caching:</strong> Purely functional synaptic memory that
              conforms to GDPR/HIPAA "Right to be Forgotten" mandates.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Seamless Dynamic Onboarding:</strong> New hospital edge clients can integrate
              into the federation without retraining historical checkpoints.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── MODULE 03 ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="module-card">
      <div class="dev-card-corner-tl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="dev-card-corner-br" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="module-header">
        <div class="module-meta">
          <span class="module-number">MODULE #03</span>
          <span class="module-badge">NESTED TOPOLOGY</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="module-name">HOPE-FL: Nested Hierarchical Edge-to-Cloud Routing</h3>
        <p class="module-lead">
          Multi-tier federated hierarchy routing model updates through decentralized cluster
          centroids to eliminate coordinator bottlenecks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="module-body-grid">
        <div class="module-feature-col">
          <h4 class="feature-title">MULTI-TIER NESTED ROUTING</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">
            In flat federated networks, hundreds of hospitals communicating simultaneously with a
            single central parameter server incur severe latency and straggler delays. HOPE-FL
            arranges edge participants into geographic and structural clusters:
          </p>
          <div class="topology-diagram-box">
            <div class="tier-level">
              <span class="tier-tag">TIER 1</span>
              <span class="tier-name">HOSPITAL EDGE NODES (Local CMS-TTT Adaptation)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tier-arrow">&darr; Local representation-level embedding sharing</div>
            <div class="tier-level">
              <span class="tier-tag">TIER 2</span>
              <span class="tier-name">REGIONAL FOG CENTROIDS (FedM3 Cluster Aggregation)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tier-arrow">&darr; Asymmetric encrypted momentum synchronization</div>
            <div class="tier-level">
              <span class="tier-tag">TIER 3</span>
              <span class="tier-name">GLOBAL COORDINATOR (Zero-Knowledge Consensus)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="module-feature-col">
          <h4 class="feature-title">HEALTHCARE &amp; SIGNAL COMPLIANCE</h4>
          <ul class="module-bullet-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Straggler Immunity:</strong> Asynchronous cluster updates allow high-bandwidth
              nodes to proceed without waiting for dropped devices.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Medical Segmentation Decathlon (MSD):</strong> Validated across 3D brain
              tumors, liver, and cardiac MRI tasks with 0.884 Mean Dice.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Provable Differential Privacy:</strong> Integrates sample-level R&eacute;nyi
              DP accounting with $(\epsilon=1.2, \delta=10^&#123;-5&#125;)$ privacy guarantees.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
